<h2 class="bde-heading-506-128 bde-heading">
Why Is Fred VanVleet on $25m in 2026-27?
</h2><div class="bde-fancy-container-506-129 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-fancy-container-506-145 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-f-text-506-158 bde-f-text">
<p>VanVleet is paid <strong>$25m</strong> because he runs an offense and defends the ball, and because he agreed to a smaller figure to stay at Houston.</p>
<ul>
<li>He won a championship at <a href="/teams/toronto-raptors/">Toronto</a> in 2019 and was an All-Star in 2022.</li>
<li>He was paid <strong>$42.85m</strong> two seasons ago, and this contract is worth about 58% of that a year.</li>
<li>He went undrafted, so his first three seasons cost Toronto almost nothing before the money caught up.</li>
<li>He is listed at 6’0″, and guards his size are usually paid less as they reach their thirties.</li>
<li>He exercised the player option on this season, which means he chose the certainty over the market.</li>
</ul>
<p>He has earned more than any undrafted player in the history of the league.</p>

</div><div class="bde-shortcode-506-159 bde-shortcode"><div class="nba-fin" data-nba-fin="why">
